    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A struct (structure) is a collection of variables (can be of different types) under a single name."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Suppose, we want to store the name, age, and salary of a person. We can do that by using 3 different variables."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "However, a better approach would be to put these data under a single name because they are data of the same person. In these situations, we can use structs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "They make our code easier to write and understand."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now that you understand why structs are used, let's see how we can create structs in C++."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Defining a structure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We use the struct keyword to define structures. Let's create a struct for our above example."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "struct Person {\n    string name;\n    int age;\n    double salary;\n};"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You can see the struct Person includes variables of 3 different types."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When we define a struct like this, we are basically creating a data type like double and int. In this example, the data type is struct Person."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, we can create variables of this struct Person type (similar to variables of int and double type)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Next, we will learn to create struct variables."
    },
